      "title": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "780f0d43-8366-543b-aa17-82eff352fbde",
      ":question/problem": "![](/tmp/course-academy-g2-readonly-tly0pcma/17592186166865/caller-moderate/generated/d55345a4168392275d665d97.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "52da5d3f-c7cf-561c-bdc6-87bcac1f020b",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "38785227-520b-57c0-b060-e587e3cc90c1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{y-1}{x+3}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "99c91bd3-8f88-58b8-b59e-7142979aa088",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{x+3}{2(y-1)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "46017d9e-6c71-58dd-87d2-61ae4f910e3b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{x+3}{y-1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d0a582ad-74ab-5d37-b53e-f07baf681613",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{x+3}{y-1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "0bef1b88-9034-5ecd-a50b-f5e102fcd570",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{2(x+3)}{y-1}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "d0a582ad-74ab-5d37-b53e-f07baf681613"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at $(-3,1)$ and has a radius of $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-3))^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={3}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+3)+2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+3}{y-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
