      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at $(0,1)$ and has a radius of $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={1}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
